  "descriptionMarkdown": "An updated version of Nytromance Games’s plan, but actually functional: Correct underground pipe and belt lengths. Intended to allow one to begin with this tier of science, can be expanded if higher spm is desired.\n\nI'm going to go ahead and call the original plan literally nonsensical - there is no way it ever could have functioned as-presented, as lines just straight-up lead to the wrong places.  This is already the hardest of the four SE sciences to set up, and having a fugazy plan doesn't help.  I repathed the whole thing.  There's a fair amount of blank space that additional machinery could go into.  It isn't the best plan, probably, but it DOES actually work.  Due to the sheer length of the plan it is likely a pump or two may be needed to connect the fluid lines to the main part of your space base due to 2.0's new fluid restrictions.\n\nPlan is intended to be deployed after Energy 1, and assumes you have Hypercooling 3 unlocked.\n\nAlso, you are going to need HUGE amounts of fertilizer to make Nutrient Gel.  Just warehouse after warehouse of the stuff.  So I hope you've been producing and stockpiling it...\n\nFactorio 2.0, Krastorio 2, Space Exploration 0.7x, stringweasel’s Valves mod, and xkyouchoux’s Space Age Building Integration mods. Should be easy to adjust without the last two.\n",
